  "summary": "The paper demonstrates three proof‑of‑concept quantum insurance workloads: (1) a simulated excess‑loss evaluation algorithm using n+2 qubits, (2) a 6‑qubit variational optimization for reinsurance allocation executed on the Wukong superconducting processor, and (3) a 4‑qubit variational QSVD solver for the Lee–Carter mortality model using a 4×4 real mortality dataset. All experiments operate on very small toy instances and focus on feasibility rather than performance advantage.",
